Phase 2 adds recovery_scans and recovery_candidates (PART 6.4).

5.4 Audit chain
• entry_hash = SHA-256 over (previous_hash || canonical JSON of the entry without hash fields). Canonical JSON: sorted keys, no extra whitespace, UTF-8.
• First entry for a user uses previous_hash = "GENESIS".
• The backend computes the hash; the database stores it. The chain is per user.
• "Verify audit chain" recomputes every hash for the current user and reports "Chain intact" or the first broken entry id.

5.5 Privacy preferences (stored in profiles.preferences)
• theme: "light" or "dark".
• keep_logs_days: 30, 90 or 365. The backend deletes operation_events older than this value for the current user when the setting is saved and at most once per hour when the dashboard loads.
• export_requested_at: timestamp or null.
• Data export (POST /api/privacy/export) builds a JSON file of the user's profile, devices, operations, events, reports and audit entries. It contains no file contents, because none are stored.
• Account deletion is NOT part of this release.


