6.2 Simulation rules (simulation.py, tested)
• Targets must be inside the managed workspace folder. Anything else returns SIMULATION_TARGET_NOT_ALLOWED.
• The run hashes each target before and after the simulation. It never opens a target for writing.
• A test asserts that no workspace file's bytes, size or modified time change during a simulation run.
• verification_status = SIMULATION_CHECK_PASSED when every target's before and after hashes match. Otherwise SIMULATION_CHECK_FAILED.
• execution_status = SIMULATION_COMPLETED when the run finished. INTERRUPTED if it stopped early.
• Report text follows PART 2.1 exactly.

6.3 Verification action
• "Re-verify" on a simulation re-hashes the same targets and compares them with the stored hashes. It writes a new event and updates verification_status only. It never changes execution_status.

6.4 Phase 2 endpoints and rules
POST /api/recovery/test-image create a ground-truth test image inside app data
POST /api/recovery/scan start a carving job (returns job id)
GET /api/jobs/{id} status and progress
GET /api/recovery/scans/{id}
GET /api/recovery/scans/{id}/candidates?type=&state=
GET /api/recovery/candidates/{id} checks, hex header, confidence components
POST /api/recovery/recover write selected candidates to the recovered folder, then re-validate

Phase 2 tables: recovery_scans (id, user_id, source_reference, status, created_at, completed_at) and recovery_candidates (id, user_id, scan_id, file_type, byte_offset, estimated_size, state, confidence, classifier_label, validation_checks jsonb, sha256). State values: DETECTED, VALIDATED, RECOVERED, VALIDATION_FAILED, WRITE_FAILED, PARTIAL.

Carving rules
• Source: only the test image in the app-data test folder. Output: only the recovered folder in app data. The backend refuses any output folder equal to or inside the source folder.
• Read in 4 MiB chunks with a 64-byte overlap. Open read-only.
• Signatures: JPEG (FF D8 FF, footer FF D9, marker structure check), PNG (89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A, IEND, CRC-32 per chunk), PDF (%PDF- to %%EOF, object and trailer check), ZIP (PK 03 04, EOCD PK 05 06 check), GIF (GIF87a or GIF89a, trailer 3B, screen descriptor check). Plain text is listed as not signature-carvable.
• Maximum candidate size 64 MiB (configurable). A JPEG or PNG with no footer inside the limit is marked PARTIAL.
• Confidence, rule-based, 0 to 100: header found +30, footer found +30, all structure checks passed +30, written output re-parsed successfully +10. The components are shown in the detail view.
• Classifier: scikit-learn RandomForestClassifier trained by scripts/train_classifier.py on generated fixtures (byte histogram, entropy, length, header and footer flags). Store the model with a version and a feature schema version. If the model is missing, return CLASSIFIER_UNAVAILABLE for classification only; carving still runs. Never describe output as a probability of recovery. Report precision, recall and F1 from its held-out split, with the note that these come from generated fixtures only.
• RECOVERED only after the output file is read back, its SHA-256 is recorded, its structure check passes again, and for images Pillow verify() passes.
• Collision policy: never overwrite. Use name_1, name_2, and so on.


